{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:Observations.WBosonMassDiscrepancy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"Observations.WBosonMassDiscrepancy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Real.Pi.Bounds"],"declarations":32,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.kappa_is_inv_chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.kappa_is_inv_chi","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L245-L248","doc":"The geometric factor κ is exactly 1/6, derived from the Euler\ncharacteristic of the Bring surface via Gauss-Bonnet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.sensitivity_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.sensitivity_range","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L231-L243","doc":"The sensitivity ∂ ln m / ∂ ln q = (q₀² + 1)/(q₀² - 1) ∈ (9, 11).\nUses q₀² ∈ (1.232, 1.233) to bound the ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.q₀_sq_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.q₀_sq_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L226-L229","doc":"q₀² is in the interval (1.232, 1.233).\nThis auxiliary lemma enables the sensitivity proof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.w_z_ratio_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.w_z_ratio_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L212-L224","doc":"The W/Z mass ratio from Markov traces is positive and less than 1.\n\n**Was an axiom credited to [jones1985]; proved 2026-09-04.** Nothing of\nJones's is needed for *these bounds*: `w_z_ratio` is a ratio of two\nMarkov traces evaluated at the decimal literal `q₀`, so the statement is\nclosed decidable arithmetic and `norm_num` discharges it. The Jones\nreference belongs on the *construction* of the Markov trace, which is\nwhere `markov_trace` cites it — not on the observation that one\nparticular quotient of it lies in `(0, 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.forward_backward_agreement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.forward_backward_agreement","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L182-L210","doc":"The predicted CDF W-boson mass shift and the observed shift agree to\nwithin a factor of two.\n\n**Was an axiom; proved 2026-09-04.** The old comment said \"full proof\nrequires `Real.pi` bounds\" — which is true and is the whole proof: the\nexpression is `K / π` for a rational `K`, and the bounds needed are\nabsurdly loose. `π > 3` gives the first conjunct and `π < 4` the second,\nso `Real.pi_gt_d6` / `Real.pi_lt_d6` are far more than enough. Nothing\nwas missing except the reduction to `K / π`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.higgs_w_ratio_exact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.higgs_w_ratio_exact","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L165-L174","doc":"The Higgs/W δq ratio equals α_s/α_W exactly — no free parameters.\nThis is because δq ∝ α; the factors (q₀-1) and 1/|χ| cancel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.w_z_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.w_z_ratio","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L159-L161","doc":"W/Z mass ratio from Markov traces: tr_M(T₁⁴)/tr_M(T₁⁶). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.markov_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.markov_trace","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L153-L157","doc":"Markov trace of T₁ⁿ in H₂(q).\nHecke generator T₁ has eigenvalues q (symmetric, dim [2]_q)\nand -q⁻¹ (antisymmetric, dim 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.qi2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.qi2","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L150-L151","doc":"Quantum integer [2]_q = q + q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.delta_m_W_observed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.delta_m_W_observed","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L145-L146","doc":"The observed CDF W mass shift in MeV. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.delta_m_W_predicted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.delta_m_W_predicted","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L140-L143","doc":"The predicted CDF W mass shift in MeV.\nδm = δq/q₀ × sensitivity × m_W. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.sensitivity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.sensitivity","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L135-L138","doc":"Logarithmic sensitivity: ∂ ln m / ∂ ln q = (q² + 1)/(q² - 1).\nDerived from the crossing energy E_× = ½(q - q⁻¹). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.delta_q_H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.delta_q_H","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L130-L131","doc":"Predicted δq for Higgs (gg→H, QCD vertex via top loop). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.delta_q_W_CDF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.delta_q_W_CDF","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L127-L128","doc":"Predicted δq for CDF W boson (qq̄→W, electroweak vertex). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.delta_q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.delta_q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L114-L123","doc":"δq is positive for positive coupling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.delta_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.delta_q","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L103-L112","doc":"Forward-predicted vertex δq with no free parameters.\n\nδq(vertex) = (q₀ - 1) × α/(2π) × 1/|χ(Σ₄)|\n\nAll three factors are determined:\n- (q₀ - 1) = 0.10998 from CODATA\n- α/(2π) = topological charge at vertex\n- 1/|χ| = 1/6 from Gauss-Bonnet on Bring surface ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.α_W_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.α_W_pos","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.α_s_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.α_s_pos","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L98-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.α_W","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.α_W","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L95-L96","doc":"Weak coupling constant: α_W = g_W²/(4π) ≈ 0.034. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.α_s","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.α_s","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L92-L93","doc":"QCD coupling constant at the Higgs mass scale. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.kappa_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.kappa_pos","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L87-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.kappa_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.kappa_val","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L84-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.kappa","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L76-L82","doc":"The geometric projection factor κ = 1/|χ(Σ₄)| = 1/6.\n\nDerivation: The S₅ automorphism group of the Bring surface forces\nconstant Webster curvature. Gauss-Bonnet fixes the total curvature\nbudget at |χ| = 6 units. A single production vertex couples to one\ncolor tube, projecting onto 1/|χ| of the total. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.abs_chi_bring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.abs_chi_bring","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L70-L72","doc":"|χ(Σ₄)| = 6. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.chi_bring_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.chi_bring_val","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.chi_bring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.chi_bring","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L64-L66","doc":"Euler characteristic of the Bring surface Σ₄ (genus g = 4).\nχ = 2 - 2g = 2 - 8 = -6. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.q₀_minus_one_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.q₀_minus_one_pos","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L61-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.q₀_minus_one_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.q₀_minus_one_val","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L58-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.q₀_minus_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.q₀_minus_one","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L55-L56","doc":"The displacement from classicality: q₀ - 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.q₀_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.q₀_pos","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L52-L53","doc":"q₀ > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.q₀_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.q₀_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L49-L50","doc":"q₀ > 1 (substrate is in the quantum regime). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WBoson.q₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WBoson.q₀","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/w-boson-mass-discrepancy.lean#L44-L47","doc":"The CODATA local substrate parameter.\nUnique root q > 1 of (1 - q⁻¹)² = Vol(4₁)/(m_μ/m_e).\nSee: QOU.Experimental.LocalSubstrateQ ","signatureChunk":0}]}